        <h2>Tips for Visiting Sri Lanka's Waterfalls</h2>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Best after the monsoon:</strong> Visit in October–December (for the south) or May–June (for the north). Dry season (January–April) can reduce some falls to trickles.</li>
          <li><strong>Footwear:</strong> Wear shoes with grip for any waterfall with a trail (Diyaluma especially). Flip flops are dangerous on wet rocks.</li>
          <li><strong>Get there early:</strong> Most popular falls (Ravana, Diyaluma roadside) are crowded from 9am. Sunrise visits are quieter.</li>
          <li><strong>Swimming safety:</strong> After heavy rain, currents in plunge pools can be surprisingly strong. Read local conditions.</li>
          <li><strong>Combined trips:</strong> Diyaluma + Ravana Falls (both on the A4 between Ella and Ratnapura), Devon + St Clair (Hatton area), Baker's Falls within the Horton Plains walk.</li>
        </ul>

